        "contenuto_esteso": "To display this content from YouTube, you must enable advertisement tracking and audience measurement. One of your browser extensions seems to be blocking the video player from loading. To watch this content, you may need to disable it on this site. French prosecutors summon Musk over allegations of child abuse images, deepfakes on X Issued on: 20/04/2026 - 11:26 Elon Musk has been summoned to Paris on Monday, where investigators are looking into allegations of misconduct related to the social media platform X, including the spread of child sexual abuse material and deepfake content. The world’s richest man and Linda Yaccarino — the former CEO of X — have been summoned for “voluntary interviews,\" while other employees of the platform are scheduled to be heard as witnesses throughout this week, the Paris prosecutor’s office said. Iran says 'no decision' on whether to attend next round of US talks 20/04/2026 US Navy seizure of Iranian ship casts doubt on fresh ceasefire talks in Pakistan 20/04/2026 Bulgaria Kremlin-friendly ex-president wins parliamentary majority 20/04/2026 Bulgaria's former President Radev takes strong lead in election 20/04/2026 UK's Starmer to face grilling from MPs over Mandelson scandal 20/04/2026 China warns joint US, Philippines and Japan drills risk regional trust 20/04/2026 'Unprecedented since 1999': Radev secures absolute majority with reformist and eurosceptic coalition 20/04/2026 Europe Bulgaria's pro-Russian former president takes strong lead 20/04/2026 Europe Ukrainian best-selling author, Andrey Kurkov speaks to France 24 19/04/2026 Europe"
